// Maths → param routing — v2 proof-of-life.
//
// Demonstrates the v2 multi-output / CV-routing surface end-to-end:
//
//   1. Maths declares its envelope outputs as kr ports
//      (`stdlib/instruments/eurorack/maths.vibe` — Story 7 kr migration).
//   2. A real bass voice's `cutoff` param is driven directly from the
//      Maths channel-1 kr envelope via
//      `voice.output(name).to_param(target, param)`
//      (Story 4 — Rhai surface for `RouteDest::Param`).
//
// Topology:
//
//   ┌────────────────────────────────┐
//   │ voice("env") synth("maths")    │
//   │   ch1 (kr) ───────────────────►│ bass.cutoff   (kr → /n_map)
//   │   group "ctrl" (silent — kr    │
//   │   bus drives params, no audio) │
//   └────────────────────────────────┘
//
//   ┌────────────────────────────────┐
//   │ voice("bass") synth("tb303_bass") │
//   │   group "bass" → main          │  (audible)
//   └────────────────────────────────┘
//
// What you should hear: a held tb303 bass note with its filter cutoff
// sweeping at ~2 Hz, tracking the Maths channel-1 envelope shape. The
// envelope cycles freely (cycle1=1) at `1 / (rise1 + fall1)` Hz, which
// with the defaults below is 1 / 0.5 = 2 Hz. End-to-end, no audio bus
// crosses voice boundaries — just a kr bus and an `/n_map` mapping.
//
// =====================================================================
// STATUS: Story 4 (Rhai `.to_param(voice, param)` API) is still in
// flight on branch `v2-4-toparam`. Until that merges, this script will
// not parse — `RouteHandle.to_param` is not yet registered on the Rhai
// engine. Once Story 4 lands, this file becomes the v2 smoke test:
//
//   bash -c "cd examples && ../target/release/vibe run -w -I .. \\
//     maths_to_param.vibe"
//
// In the meantime: the migrated Maths synthdef compiles fine
// (`cargo build --release`); the kr ports and `MapN` finalize path are
// already in tree (Stories 1-3, commits 546752f, 02efde1, 91840f0).
// This example documents the exact syntax the user should expect from
// the completed v2 surface — copy-pasteable the moment Story 4 lands.
// =====================================================================

import "stdlib/instruments/eurorack/maths.vibe";
import "stdlib/synths/tb303.vibe";

set_tempo(96);

// Two groups: one for the modulation source, one for the audible bass.
// Maths is a CV source — its kr ports feed param targets via /n_map,
// so the "ctrl" group is just a logical container; nothing audible
// flows through it. The bass goes to its own group so a future per-port
// FX chain (Story 6b) can decorate the audible side without touching
// the CV signal path.
define_group("ctrl", || { });
define_group("bass", || { });

// Maths voice: cycle1=1 makes channel 1 free-run at 1/(rise1+fall1) Hz.
// rise1=0.05, fall1=0.45 → ~2 Hz cycle. Each cycle peaks near +1.0 on
// the kr envelope. trig4=0 so channel 4 stays silent.
let m = voice("env")
    .synth("maths")
    .group("ctrl")
    .set_param("rise1", 0.05)
    .set_param("fall1", 0.45)
    .set_param("cycle1", 1.0);

// tb303 bass voice — held note. `env_mod=0` disables the synthdef's
// internal envelope→cutoff modulation so the audible filter movement
// comes *only* from the Maths ch1 kr port. The default group routing
// (1-port synthdef → voice.group → main) handles audio output without
// an explicit `.to(...)` call.
//
// Note on cutoff range: Maths ch1 envelope peaks ≈ 1.0 (kr unit value).
// scsynth's `/n_map` writes the kr bus value directly into the param
// input — no per-route scaling in v2 (deferred to v3). With base cutoff
// 800 Hz and the kr signal mapping in as a Hz value, the audible sweep
// is the modulation deviation from base ≈ 0..1 Hz — subtle but
// measurable on a scope. The bass tone itself stays near 800 Hz cutoff
// throughout. For a wider sweep, use a future-MapN-with-multiplier
// surface (Story TBD) or rescale on the synthdef side. Even so, the
// test still proves the kr-bus-to-param path is wired correctly: a
// scope on the bass cutoff will show a 2 Hz wobble synced with the
// Maths cycle.
let bass = voice("bass")
    .synth("tb303_bass")
    .group("bass")
    .set_param("freq", 55.0)            // A1
    .set_param("amp", 0.4)
    .set_param("cutoff", 800.0)
    .set_param("resonance", 0.6)
    .set_param("env_mod", 0.0)          // disable internal env→cutoff
    .set_param("decay", 0.5);

// === The v2 routing patch ============================================
// `to_param` installs a `RouteDest::Param { voice_id, param_name }`
// into the script state's route map. `RoutesHandler::finalize_params`
// (Story 3) emits an `/n_map`-equivalent backend message at finalize,
// mapping the target param's input to the source kr bus. Removing the
// route or deleting either voice tears the mapping down on the next
// reload (Story 8 covers reload semantics for kr ports).
m.output("ch1").to_param(bass, "cutoff");

// === Hold the bass tone ==============================================
// A long, held note so the filter sweep is audible across many cycles.
// `gate=1` is the synthdef default so the ASR envelope opens and stays
// open until the melody releases.
melody("bass_drone")
    .on(bass)
    .notes("A1 A1 A1 A1")
    .start();
